  "report": {
    "executive_summary": "The disturbance was initiated at 16:50:44 BST by lightning on the Blyth–Eccles–Stella West circuit [I01]; the Eaton Socon–Wymondley circuit then faulted again on re-energisation [I02]. Hornsea lost 400 MW and Little Barford's three units tripped [I10, I11, I12, I13]. The frequency was arrested at 49.1 Hz, fell to 48.8 Hz, returned to 50 Hz at 16:57 and was below 49 Hz for 16 seconds [I20, I21, I22, I23]. The ST1C trip was caused by a faulty speed sensor and GT1A by a failed bypass valve [I30, I31]; the Hornsea de-load was caused by its reactive compensator [I32].",
    "sections": [
      {
        "body": "See [I01, I02, I03, I10, I11, I12, I13]. Frequency: [I20, I21, I22, I23]. Causes: [I30, I31, I32].",
